                  <syl /><neume facs="#m-8bac2948-1e00-40f5-97c2-5a77e0dd7a7a" type="punctum" xml:id="m-b09b514a-bc0d-4d90-9a94-631ac6da240d">
                    <nc xml:id="m-3a1f7dd8-260e-44f8-8ec2-994c912073bd" pname="f" oct="3" />
                  </neume>
                </syllable>
              </layer>
            </staff>
            <div xml:id="m-fc4b1f01-4a43-43a7-b9a7-0f415824e744">
              <lg xml:id="m-37a36f5e-32bd-4312-a35d-3ba9e849c49d">
                <l xml:id="m-e17e8c60-e1b0-4b76-b3f1-75634f2f0869" facs="#m-b465e6f6-abfd-477f-b616-2f62ac9fb4a8" label="text-like">The Solemn afternoon Liturgy</l><l xml:id="m-e2a04e85-5951-4825-8466-5e7eba2d012f" facs="#m-c7626fe8-b094-4559-9878-c0a4672c8c01" label="ambiguous">735</l><l xml:id="m-cffffd07-4673-4ae2-9a9a-6535d9670070" facs="#m-245f6fcd-cac5-49aa-ac56-40d2fc626749" label="text-like">FOR THE CONVERSION OF THE HEATHEN</l><l xml:id="m-03ab4736-e293-4619-9d32-e28db53f4cd3" facs="#m-44326d7b-2dcd-4be1-8bb1-f0d4f24c9b84" label="lyrics-like">Rémus et pro pagánis: ut Deus omnípotens áuferat iniquitátem</l><l xml:id="m-051a6fc5-3e6d-48e8-adbf-10b10bc13063" facs="#m-792316db-e274-49da-a2b1-4e162647cfa9" label="lyrics-like">U a córdibus eórum; ut, relictis idólis suis, convertántur ad</l><l xml:id="m-79d2c2eb-b0ea-4803-a2c6-b66a05dc92a7" facs="#m-0bb49b99-df44-4538-acb0-81561d025e51" label="lyrics-like">Deum vivum et verum, et únicum Filium ejus Jesum Christum,</l><l xml:id="m-abb4d6e3-a703-44fd-8922-8a1d6e1e5da0" facs="#m-cd3106c3-8e43-4b86-88e1-989f79c71337" label="lyrics-like">Deum et Dóminum nostrum.</l><l xml:id="m-d0a57053-6c84-49d6-9078-08720b88702e" facs="#m-5411bb03-236c-45f5-a287-05d940c3cffc" label="lyrics-like">C. Orémus. D. Flectámus génua. D. Leváte.</l><l xml:id="m-5593774c-48a1-4083-8a31-c30a58a7472d" facs="#m-c0267fa0-ca0f-4edf-999a-15eb1cd96733" label="lyrics-like">Mnipotens sempitérne Deus, l cultúra; * et ággrega Ecclésiae</l><l xml:id="m-7a85b4f5-2dca-4cd3-affb-c85404b2065a" facs="#m-b8dc2955-2ea6-4d9c-93c8-f29152983455" label="lyrics-like">U qui non mortem peccatórum, l tuae sanctae, ad laudem et gló¬</l><l xml:id="m-f9d5e1ec-7e4e-4bf2-b36a-673dd7908912" facs="#m-e26470e6-e141-4b92-9a4a-92a38e9d8616" label="lyrics-like">sed vitam semper inquíris:</l><l xml:id="m-20143156-6859-403d-b520-289e9e0f4fdb" facs="#m-0b5b327a-7674-43d3-b061-b096347bd13e" label="lyrics-like">riam nóminis tui. Per Dóminum</l><l xml:id="m-b87c3331-f0fc-482a-bbb4-32fb3b03c220" facs="#m-cbd90600-3fc4-4eda-944c-1e9b20313db6" label="lyrics-like">súscipe propítius oratiónem no- nostrum Jesum Christum.</l><l xml:id="m-26a896cc-763e-4379-931e-c290d3dcdfda" facs="#m-5e7db64f-12d6-4fab-a97a-56858cdffe0e" label="lyrics-like">stram, et libera eos ab idolórum!</l><l xml:id="m-c4ab2b0f-fa6e-4050-bcd6-32b2d4305062" facs="#m-c3d6776e-caf1-4e57-a28f-be44dc52b5e2" label="ambiguous">Al: K. Amen.</l><l xml:id="m-80d072aa-c8e0-4b70-b7de-09a3bbceeafe" facs="#m-b556ed4f-69d2-4694-9db9-16a63e8bc539" label="text-like">THIRD PART OF THE LITURGY:</l><l xml:id="m-20e1d74c-8dd3-40d0-affe-eea17446276f" facs="#m-444537f9-17be-47e6-bd96-2a67ba0832d2" label="text-like">THE ADORATION OF THE HOLY CROSS</l><l xml:id="m-3b0a5fc7-69b9-4500-8433-1663e6a7d51d" facs="#m-95227424-063e-4888-8dac-2b04b80b8c25" label="text-like">14. After the solemn collects, the celebrant and ministers Ior serversl, bowing</l><l xml:id="m-1e74f8bf-9806-4880-a7b3-b1499b92a6fc" facs="#m-08f8ad31-bf75-43aa-b5a1-791e524513e9" label="lyrics-like">to the altar, go back to the sedilia by the shortest way : the celebrant t̃akes oñ</l><l xml:id="m-f5579188-804c-44c8-8218-61118a4ad8f7" facs="#m-009c8967-676a-4431-aee3-8c4c1432aa5a" label="text-like">his cope, the ministers the dalmatic and tunicle: the solemn adoration of the</l><l xml:id="m-92974243-885e-423d-b228-b082de6e29ba" facs="#m-b154507e-27a1-4942-80f8-8fb27608d747" label="ambiguous">Cross then begins.</l><l xml:id="m-5bb159fa-ecd2-466b-89d8-b3191ae614b1" facs="#m-5cf5bf37-7eb5-4520-bcef-99a3578a4921" label="text-like">A large Cross is used whose figure is covered by a purple veil which can be</l><l xml:id="m-fc00dce1-b030-4bb2-9452-a9abcac4abc3" facs="#m-334051a5-da62-40e7-8bd3-c6516aa409d0" label="ambiguous">easily removed.</l><l xml:id="m-2ac54926-a656-407f-8d13-d3f827821ea9" facs="#m-68bc763d-f9a8-447d-a67c-e79566ce95c3" label="text-like">15. The Cross is first brought from the sacristy to the middle of the sanctuary,</l><l xml:id="m-d7b968b8-4ab0-4e1f-a509-2400328a4c82" facs="#m-03ff5b16-47c5-468b-954b-4f527619a93d" label="text-like">while all stand. It is carried in this way : the celebrant and the subdeacon</l><l xml:id="m-2c5f8a25-ac10-4464-82f9-38d39c10f758" facs="#m-efe2e17d-bb14-4668-a5a3-1e729089ef96" label="text-like">stay at their bench, standing; the deacon goes to the sacristy with the acolytes</l><l xml:id="m-1f2e8ce9-db86-4966-9619-60bb52630fee" facs="#m-0904e3b0-9f0c-48f1-935f-c5338a0f6576" label="text-like">Ior serversl and from there he brings the Cross in procesmion io the church.</l><l xml:id="m-c1dbcf91-6a02-459e-9f86-9363ff594c8d" facs="#m-ad0aec39-543d-4139-9367-899c1b75de79" label="text-like">The acolytes for serversl go first, ihen the deacon with the Cross, walking</l><l xml:id="m-87c8f7bd-770f-43e9-b691-54a5fa4e0637" facs="#m-24181009-1fc4-403c-9a89-133192543d7b" label="ambiguous">between two more acolytes lor serversl who carry lighted candles.</l><l xml:id="m-eb77e8a4-61ac-4822-bba0-a79540549de5" facs="#m-92110f88-0aa0-4634-9290-c9c0f98645f4" label="text-like">When they reach the sanctuary, the celebrant and subdeacon go to meet</l><l xml:id="m-f996d044-3686-4d38-9146-bb6721b15742" facs="#m-803d2bf3-495b-4a5b-8f60-2fedaa15289f" label="text-like">them, and the celebrant receives the Cross in the middle, in front of the altar.</l><l xml:id="m-3223757c-5313-40dc-a48f-7aba38d96b40" facs="#m-6cc87341-9521-4d9b-8f17-de229664dc23" label="text-like">I15a. The celebrant goes to the sacristy with the servers and from there</l><l xml:id="m-e4c8547c-8120-473c-835c-98ee6197be25" facs="#m-a05d5f69-055d-4e33-a790-bf46c65c8dcd" label="text-like">brings in the Cross, as abovel.</l><l xml:id="m-d4c95d0b-b692-4f6e-95da-3acdeb7b547c" facs="#m-48cb721e-0ea8-4d57-8b37-fa18f3dc6689" label="text-like">16. The holy Cross is then unveiled in this way:</l><l xml:id="m-6ff50108-2111-4944-9c4e-2e6e6e0634a2" facs="#m-87cc7b3e-af79-4cd5-b851-bdf27fd39dd8" label="text-like">The celebrant, holding the Cross, with deacon and subdeacon [first and</l><l xml:id="m-8248607a-4521-40de-bf4e-3bbf55dde297" facs="#m-741d5f44-174b-4729-920c-e53763f06b44" label="text-like">second servers! on either side, and two acolytes [serversl with lighted candles,</l><l xml:id="m-19dbe9ba-6e29-42bd-9fa7-eee9be117f0e" facs="#m-3a77c628-fbc0-494b-9764-95a70734a683" label="lyrics-like">goes to the Epistle side on floor-level, stands facing thé people, and uncovers</l><l xml:id="m-c4a671b5-0389-4a36-9580-06e8cb241505" facs="#m-e76322e5-5c71-405b-8281-d9dddec04762" label="text-like">the top of the cross a litile. An acolyte [serverl holds the book; the celebrant</l><l xml:id="m-eeff04eb-6137-4190-951b-4989d26cf189" facs="#m-699c68cc-c894-4dd9-b9f9-6bf5156a6a70" label="lyrics-like">mones alone, at a lou puch, Ecce lignum Crúcis, and the sacred ministers</l><l xml:id="m-122a5462-01c1-4cf8-bc09-74914e23f595" facs="#m-16291ada-fed2-4972-881f-32c39f067f63" label="lyrics-like">sing it with him as far as Venite, adorémus, which is sung by the schola and</l><l xml:id="m-dc1a4f7d-9775-48c9-9f63-64eb34ba7d7f" facs="#m-dc6bc4ad-701a-45e6-9391-0f030f214f70" label="text-like">all the people, standing.</l><l xml:id="m-42302c73-c498-4393-bd52-35144007bca5" facs="#m-b47f001c-38f6-4e66-a920-1692c7d2c561" label="text-like">IIn the simple rite, the celebrant alone sings or reads the antiphon as far as</l><l xml:id="m-4ba6f49d-a463-4007-bc27-991d2c74221e" facs="#m-ac723397-c7cb-4801-85a5-0eb023d0577c" label="lyrics-like">Venite, adorémus, ahich is sung by alll.</l><l xml:id="m-715be76c-0097-4c89-89c4-ad248b05bb5f" facs="#m-657c52ee-62e7-4efa-9636-4c412bf8d19e" label="text-like">ANTIPHON AT THE UNVEILING OF THE CROSS</l><l xml:id="m-e9a53847-4b9c-4678-b206-cf89fbb36601" facs="#m-24bdb629-15eb-42dd-bd28-b4d3425bc57a" label="text-like">The ministers with the celebrant</l><l xml:id="m-fcdf110b-e454-4955-ab97-7c64ebe653d3" facs="#m-4d1a6be2-cc45-4c2a-a9ae-b84c2d39def1" label="text-like">The celebrant</l><l xml:id="m-0e6fc34c-381b-47f9-90bc-d9298cc9b3b2" facs="#m-b78f4798-499f-4274-bbf8-c511b9f0be6e" label="ambiguous">M</l><l xml:id="m-152d7e5d-0373-4a38-984f-1f0c733046b7" facs="#m-f6107408-3018-4926-8d62-f783ce58ad05" label="lyrics-like">Cce lí-gnum Crú¬cis,</l><l xml:id="m-be7b4de7-63e2-4c54-99ca-97f3f4bf178c" facs="#m-0935adcc-87fa-49b1-8555-5c4943493353" label="lyrics-like">in quo sá-lus mún¬</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>